      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should we fix sh_binary to support vendor variants?",
      "revId": "ef4406ad442aadd8f0c943f3d50da7ee9a824e69",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9eeda786_97e17372",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-24T01:17:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "An alternative is to actually mutate sh_binary by the image mutator.",
      "revId": "ef4406ad442aadd8f0c943f3d50da7ee9a824e69",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8e8394a1_be74d2e5",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-24T01:38:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIRC, that was Sundong\u0027s first attempt.\n\nIn fact, sh_binary is mutated by the \"image\" mutator (that\u0027s why the existing apexes can have sh_binary modules via \"binaries\" property). The problem is sh_binary doesn\u0027t create \"vendor.*\" variants while being mutated by the \"image\" mutator. Making \"vendor.*\" variants is quite complex. We might need to move bunch of those logic out of cc package and use it. Or, we can just create all vendor.* variants with possible values.\n\nbtw, creating vendor.* variants for sh_binary modules doesn\u0027t make sense to me.",
      "parentUuid": "9eeda786_97e17372",
      "revId": "ef4406ad442aadd8f0c943f3d50da7ee9a824e69",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ab0b07b0_308d679a",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-24T01:38:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I found that prebuilt_etc is in the similar situation. prebuilt_etc modules are mutated by \"image\" variants, but not creating vendor.* variants. Apexes add dependency to prebuilt_etc modules with not specifying \"image\" variation.",
      "parentUuid": "5d928e0b_03b75e5b",
      "revId": "ef4406ad442aadd8f0c943f3d50da7ee9a824e69",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "56342472_487becbf",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-24T01:49:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Then I think the best way forward is to not allow sh_binary modules to be listed in the binaries property, and force them to be in the new sh_binaries property.",
      "parentUuid": "8e8394a1_be74d2e5",
      "revId": "ef4406ad442aadd8f0c943f3d50da7ee9a824e69",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
